# Backend Rules

## Architecture

- Follow the layered architecture:
  Routes → Controllers → Services → Repositories → Prisma → PostgreSQL
- Controllers handle only HTTP concerns.
- Services contain business logic.
- Repositories contain all Prisma queries.
- Never access Prisma directly from controllers.

## Project Structure

- Keep controllers, services, repositories, middleware, validators, and routes in separate modules.
- Keep validation reusable and isolated.

## API

- Return JSON responses only.
- Use consistent error responses through the global error handler.
- Throw custom application errors instead of generic errors.

## Business Logic

- Keep all business rules in the service layer.
- Keep status transition logic in a dedicated validator.
- Treat the backend as the source of truth.

## Validation

- Validate all client input on the backend.
- Never rely on frontend validation alone.

## Database

- Access data only through repositories.
- Never use raw SQL with user input.

## Scope

Do not implement:
- Authentication
- Authorization
- User CRUD
- Pagination
- Audit logs
- Features outside the specification.